messages:
cal: Opening a small PR to reconcile quota/rate-limit examples across pricing, metering, and SDK snippets. Main changes: replace any remaining `x-rw-usage` samples with `x-rw-consumption`, show formula-based pricing (no hard numbers), add short Go+JS examples for parsing nested tiers, and fix the console dashboard permalink. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/6120

mina: Thanks Cal. Please include a short 'quick check' snippet that shows how to decide batch size using remaining burst credits. Customers ask for a one-liner rule.

cal: Good idea. Planning to include a 2-row table with variables and a tiny python one-liner: `batch = min(max_batch, remaining_burst // avg_tokens_per_request)`. Will also add a short ascii flow: check -> compute -> send.

arthur: Heads-up: SDKs now return `consumption.tiers` as an array and also include `consumption.summary.normalized_remaining`. Examples should prefer `summary` then fall back to scanning tiers. Also note that header name changed to `x-rw-consumption` in the runtime last quarter.

sophie: Legal reminder: avoid publishing explicit pricing numbers; use `cost_per_unit` variables and link to the pricing matrix. Also please include an eventual-consistency note (~30-90s) for quota endpoints.

cal: Updated PR: switched to variables, added fallback parse pattern for Go/JS/Python, included the batch-choice one-liner, and added the eventual-consistency caveat. Example parse snippet (JS):

```js
// prefer summary, otherwise scan tiers
const data = await resp.json();
let remaining = data.consumption?.summary?.normalized_remaining;
if (remaining == null) {
  remaining = (data.consumption?.tiers || []).reduce((s,t)=> s + (t.remaining||0), 0);
}
```

mina: That looks great. Can you also add a short curl example for support teams and include the panel UID/permalink for the Grafana view so infra can confirm perms?

cal: Added curl and the panel permalink (panel-usage-9c). I pinged eng-infra to confirm access for hosted customers.

docs-bot: PR opened by cal: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/6120 — reviewers: @mina, @arthur. CI checks queued: linkcheck, snippet-lint, spellcheck.

arthur: Reviewed and left one small comment about handling missing fields defensively. No blockers from engineering.

mina: Approved after minor wording tweak.

cal: Merged once CI green and infra confirmed permalink. Follow-ups: backport to release/1.x, post short migration blurb in #release-notes, and open a tiny SDK PR to update header parsing examples. Closing thread. :tada:
